msgid "Table 1 of the same paper: uniform monoenergetic electron sources in the same spheres, from 0.01 to 1000 g and from 0.1 to 4 MeV (133 values, in `validation/stabin2000_electrons.csv`). The rows at 4 MeV came out scrambled in the text extraction of the PDF and were reassembled by hand; every row was checked against the EGS4/MCNP mean. The model is the one used for photons, with `particle = electron` and 10⁵ histories per case. The radius comes from the mass, since the table rounds it to 0.01 cm."
